    "result_text": "The full test suite is green. Only one test class exists (`AcceptanceTest`), and it passes along with the whole build.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `capacityWarning` flag so it returns `true` when the owner's city already holds between 40 and 49 owners (approaching the hard limit of 50), leaving the existing 50-owner hard rejection unchanged.\n\nChanges:\n\n1. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 Added the read-only `capacityWarning` boolean property to the Owner schema, so the generated `OwnerDto` carries the field.\n\n2. **`model/Owner.java`** \u2014 Added the `capacityWarning` column field with getter/setter, mirroring `bulkSignupWarning`. MapStruct maps it to the DTO by name automatically.\n\n3. **`OwnerRestControllerV1.java`** \u2014 Added a `CAPACITY_WARNING_THRESHOLD = 40` constant and an `assignCapacityWarning(owner)` method (called during `addOwner`, right after `assignBulkSignupWarning`). It counts pre-existing owners in the city case-insensitively \u2014 the same way `rejectCityAtCapacity` does \u2014 and sets the flag `true` when the count is `>= 40 && < 50`. Because the hard-limit check (`>= 50` \u2192 409) runs earlier in the pipeline, this only ever evaluates below the limit.\n\n4. **Schema files** (hsqldb/h2/mysql/postgres `schema.sql`) \u2014 Added the `capacity_warning BOOLEAN` column to the `owners` table.\n\nThe new acceptance test `coreWarnsWhenApproachingCapacity` (fill a city to 40, then the 41st owner warns) passes, and `BUILD SUCCESS` with 0 failures/errors.",
